d output tools to move a project from screen to print; attend a workshop if you need print guidance.","short_summary":"A production-centered workspace for large-format, photo, and color-laser output.","evidence_claim":"Pratt’s 2D Printing Center is its centralized output area for color laser, professional photo, and large-format printing, with file-preparation instruction and scanning.","source_url":"https://www.pratt.edu/services/2d-printing-center/","source_title":"2D Printing Center","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Listed hours are 8:30 AM–midnight daily; printing beyond the stated semester allotment uses Pratt Card funds.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"pratt-3d-printing-center","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"3D Printing Center","title":"3D Printing Center","subtitle":"Engineering Building, 2nd Floor, Room 211","notes":"Bring a prepared STL file for prototyping or consult the center’s guidance before submitting; scanning is available by approved appointment.","short_summary":"A cross-disciplinary prototyping workspace with 3D printers and scanners.","evidence_claim":"The 3D Printing Center is open to students and staff of all disciplines and provides 3D printing and 3D scanning for stages from prototyping to presentation-quality prints.","source_url":"https://www.pratt.edu/services/3d-printing-center/","source_title":"3D Printing Center","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Listed hours vary by day; files are submitted through OnePratt and 3D-print charges are approved before production. Scans require manager approval and an appointment.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"pratt-pmc-open-computer-lab-508","subject_type":"study_s